 — joint US Department of Defense / NASA mission. Originally designed to test SDI (Strategic Defense Initiative) sensors against an asteroid, with the Moon as a calibration target. First US lunar mission after Apollo 17 (21 years).",{"met_days":55,"type":56,"label":57,"description":58},9,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-lunar injection","1994-02-03, after an eight-day checkout in low Earth orbit. The STAR 37FM solid motor sent Clementine into a phasing loop that passed Earth twice before reaching the Moon.",{"met_days":60,"type":61,"label":62,"description":63},10,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TLI cleanup.",{"met_days":65,"type":61,"label":66,"description":67},10.24,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":69,"type":61,"label":70,"description":71},12.75,"TCM-3 — final pre-LOI","Final approach targeting before lunar orbit insertion.",{"met_days":12,"type":73,"label":74,"description":75},"arrival","Lunar approach","Pre-LOI checkout phase.",{"met_days":77,"type":78,"label":79,"description":80},25.05,"edl_or_oi","Lunar orbit insertion","1994-02-19. Captured into a 415 × 2,940 km polar orbit. Mapped the lunar surface at multiple wavelengths over 71 days — first global high-resolution multispectral lunar map. Bi-static radar experiment data was later interpreted (controversially) as evidence of water ice at the lunar south pole — a disputed hint that spurred later ice searches.",{"source_tier":82,"parking_orbit":83,"tli":87,"translunar":89,"lunar_arrival":91,"return":93,"waypoints_km":95},"tier_1_5_hybrid",{"altitude_km":84,"inclination_deg":85,"revs":86},250,67,2,{"dv_kms":88},3.05,{"type":90},"direct",{"type":92,"altitude_km":41,"inclination_deg":42,"periselene_km":41},"orbit",{"type":94},"none",[96,98,101,106,111,116,121,126,131,136,141,146,151,156,161,166,171,176,181,186,191,196,201,206,211,216,221,226,231,236,241,246,251,256,261,262,266,270,274,277,280,284,288,292,296,300,304,308,312,315,319,323,327,331,335,339,343,347,351,355,358,362,366,370,374,378,382,386,390,394,398,402,406,41